nv30: validate the index buffer's binding before the indexed draw

On NV40_3D an indexed draw with a real index buffer binds it through the buffer
context: PUSH_RESRC/PUSH_MTHD register the method in the bufctx and write
bo->offset + data inline using whatever offset is known right now, which is 0
for a buffer this submission has not validated yet.

libdrm's pushbuf_validate() is what turns that into a real address. It walks
bctx->pending and, for every ref carrying a ->packet, appends the (method
header, value) relocation pair that the kernel patches at submit time, then
drains pending into current.

The only validation an indexed draw got ran inside nv30_state_validate(), which
nv30_draw_vbo() calls before nv30_draw_elements(). So by the time the index
buffer is bound, validation for this draw has already happened. Its relocation
pair is never emitted, and IDXBUF_OFFSET reaches the engine as a bare,
unrelocated resource offset -- 0x00000100 on the machine this was found on,
which is not even page aligned. The engine fetches indices out of unrelated
video memory and the garbage indices drive vertex fetches far past the end of
the vertex array bound at VTXBUF0/VTXBUF1: DMA_VTX_PROTECTION, on every
indexed VBO draw, deterministically.

The vertex and fragment-program bindings are registered during state validation
and so are covered by that same validate, which is why they alone come back
correctly relocated in the very same push -- a controlled comparison inside one
submission.

Validating again after the binding, before the draw is emitted, is enough.

Measured on a GeForce 7600 GS (NV4B, class 4097) with mesa-demos:
  stock  -- 16 relocations in the faulting push, none for IDXBUF, 1 fault/run
  fixed  -- 20 relocations, including the pairs whose constants decode to
            0004f81c (IDXBUF_OFFSET) and 0004f820 (IDXBUF_FORMAT),
            and 0 faults over 12 consecutive runs, no kernel oops

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_vbo.c	2026-09-07 10:10:59.772566855 +0000
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_vbo.c	2026-09-07 10:43:54.068128328 +0000
@@ -489,6 +489,16 @@
                        (index_size == 2) ? 0x00000010 : 0x00000000,
                        res->domain | NOUVEAU_BO_RD,
                        0, NV30_3D_IDXBUF_FORMAT_DMA1);
+      /* The index buffer is bound through the buffer context, which defers its
+       * relocation to pushbuf validation -- and nv30_state_validate(), the only
+       * validation this draw would otherwise get, has already run by the time we
+       * get here. Without validating again the relocation pair is never emitted
+       * for this submission, and IDXBUF_OFFSET reaches the engine as a bare,
+       * unrelocated resource offset. The engine then fetches indices from
+       * unrelated memory and the garbage indices drive vertex fetches past the
+       * end of the vertex array: DMA_VTX_PROTECTION. */
+      if (PUSH_VAL(push))
+         return;
       BEGIN_NV04(push, NV30_3D(VERTEX_BEGIN_END), 1);
       PUSH_DATA (push, prim);
       while (count) {
